[size=3][b]📝 Mod Author Notes:[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][size=3][size=3]You [b][i][u]MUST[/u][/i] [/b]have an appropriate modid in the mod.manifest for your mod. You [b][i][u]MUST[/u][/i] [/b]use only lowercase letters and underscores in the modid (no number, spaces, or other special characters). You should also make your mod's folder name the same as your modid as a fallback if there is a problem parsing the mod.manifest file. You should be doing this anyway if your mod contains a pak since the pak name must match the modid and the folder name. [color=#ea9999][b]This is a requirement of how the game is programmed to handle mods and is NOT optional. [/b][/color][/size][/size][/*]
[*][size=3][b][color=#ffe599]FOMOD Authors - [/color][/b]Make sure your file output includes a top level folder. So if your mod contains mod.manifest and a "Data" folder, make sure you include a folder with a name matching the modid from the mod.manifest above those files. Otherwise, the mod will not be entered into the mod_order.txt Load Order file and will not be loaded by the game. [/size][/*]
[/list]
